    "durationMs": 533771,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and verified. Summary of what's in `/workspace`:\n\n- **Laravel 11** (PHP 8.3) scaffolded with `vendor/` installed; `bootstrap/app.php` registers `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''`, so paths are `/links`, `/r/{code}` — no `/api` prefix.\n- **`app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php`** — manual validation returning `{\"error\": ...}` for 422 (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code), 409 on duplicate code, 404 on unknown code; `GET /r/{code}` returns a 302 with the exact stored `Location` and does one atomic `clicks + 1`; list is ordered by id ascending with `total`.\n- **`app/Models/Link.php` + migration** — `links` table (unique `code` 4–20 chars, `url`, `clicks`), persisted in MySQL with credentials read only from `DB_*` env vars (nothing DB-related in `.env`).\n- **`start.sh`** (executable, POSIX sh) — retries `php artisan migrate --force`, then `exec php artisan serve --no-reload --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000`.\n- **README** — \"Running the server\" section with `sh start.sh`.\n\nVerified with a 58-check curl suite (all passing) plus a full restart-persistence test, a clean-DB smoke run through every endpoint, and `route:list` confirming no `/api` prefix. I left the database empty and port 8000 free so `sh start.sh` can be run fresh by the test harness."
